    basic: "Don't blink! The cards are moving so fast that beginners often get 'Tunnel Vision' looking at their own hand. Your peripheral vision is your greatest assetâ€”watch the person directly across from you, not just your cards. If you see them freeze or reach for their face, react immediately even if you don't know who has the set.",
    intermediate: "The 'Slow Pass': If you have 3 cards of a rank, you only need one more. Stop passing quickly. Wait for the person to your right to drop a card. This allows you to focus 100% on other players' faces. If you rush the pass, you might miss the subtle finger-to-nose movement of the winner.",
    advanced: "The 'Fake-Out': If you are playing with veterans, try scratching your nose or adjusting your glasses. This often triggers a 'Panic Reaction' where everyone touches their noses. You get to laugh at them for being jumpy, and it masks your real win later in the round. Subtlety is the difference between a pro Pig player and a loser.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If you are the one who completed the 4-of-a-kind, try to wait 2 or 3 seconds before touching your nose. Let the panic of the passing cards build first.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If playing the 'Spoons' variation, grab the spoon softly. The sound of a clattering spoon ruins the surprise.",
      },
